  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women Entrepreneurship Development and Access to Finance Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promote access to finance and growth for women entrepreneurs in Benin</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed Operation has two main results areas in order to achieve the PDO: RA I:  Enhance women entrepreneurial skills and mindsetRA II: Increase women entrepreneurs access to financeThe term &#x2018;women entrepreneurs in this operation refers to micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (formal and informal) owned by a female (sole proprietorships or at least 51 percent of the share) or led by women as the main managing person responsible of the business. The promotion of &#x2018;growth&#x2019; refers both to an increase in the overall number of formal women entrepreneurs in the economy, the improvement in employment outcomes&#x2014;such as the creation of new quality jobs&#x2014;among W-MSMEs supported by this operation, access to new markets and increase business income. The promotion of &#x2018;access to finance for W-MSMEs encompasses both the number of W-MSMEs gaining access to financial services and the volume of mobilized private capital.</narrative>
  </description>
